'''Kubi''' (also known as Kuba, Kubawa) is an extinct [[Afro-Asiatic languages|Afro-Asiatic]] language formerly spoken in [[Bauchi State]], [[Nigeria]]. Members of the ethnic group now speak [[Hausa language|Hausa]].<ref name=e25/>

Kubi is a village that is known as a member of the Za'ar tribe and also speaks the same language.

